### TopUp Wallet — Wallet.Api
### The money core: accounts, idempotent credit/debit, ledger, audit.
### Every endpoint (except /health) requires a JWT access token as a Bearer
### header. Run top-to-bottom: the first request logs in (on Auth.Api) and the
### token + account id chain into the rest automatically.
###
### Container ports (compose): auth :5003, wallet :5001. Local `dotnet run` may
### pick other ports — override the @vars below if needed.

@auth   = http://localhost:5003
@host   = http://localhost:5001
@contentType = application/json

### Health (open, no token)
GET {{host}}/health

###
# @name login
### Get a token first. Any non-empty username/password works (demo).
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "any-non-empty"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Unauthenticated call -> 401 (no Bearer header on purpose)
POST {{host}}/accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "ownerName": "No Auth", "currency": "USD", "opening": 10 }

###
# @name createAccount
### Create an account (owned by the logged-in user). Token required.
POST {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "ownerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "currency": "USD",
  "opening": 100
}

###
@accountId = {{createAccount.response.body.$.id}}

### Fetch the account (only the owner can)
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Credit $50
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/credit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "amount": 50, "idempotencyKey": "credit-001" }

### Debit $30
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "amount": 30, "idempotencyKey": "debit-001" }

### Idempotency — REPLAY the same debit key.
### Expect: wasReplay=true, SAME transactionId, balance unchanged.
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "amount": 30, "idempotencyKey": "debit-001" }

### Insufficient funds -> 400 { "error": "insufficient_funds" }
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "amount": 999999, "idempotencyKey": "debit-overdraw" }

### Validation — non-positive amount -> 400
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/credit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "amount": 0, "idempotencyKey": "credit-zero" }

### Immutable ledger (SQL Server), newest first
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit trail (MongoDB), append-only
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ================= FUNDING (money IN via payment gateway) =================
### Fund the wallet from a card. The browser tokenizes the card with the PSP;
### here we pass a demo token. Money is credited on the SIGNED WEBHOOK, not here.
###   tok_ok      -> Succeeded (webhook will credit)
###   tok_decline -> Declined
###   tok_3ds     -> RequiresAction (3-D Secure) + clientSecret

###
# @name createDeposit
### Create a $100 deposit. Response: depositId + status. Deposit is PENDING —
### balance is NOT credited yet.
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "paymentToken": "tok_ok", "amount": 100 }

###
@depositId = {{createDeposit.response.body.$.depositId}}

### Balance still unchanged (webhook not received yet)
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# @name webhookPayload
### DEMO helper: returns a correctly-SIGNED webhook body + signature for this
### deposit, so you can fire the webhook below without a real PSP calling back.
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits/{{depositId}}/webhook-payload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@webhookBody = {{webhookPayload.response.body.$.body}}
@webhookSig  = {{webhookPayload.response.body.$.signature}}

### PSP WEBHOOK (open endpoint — authenticated by HMAC signature, not a JWT).
### Valid signature -> wallet credited. Balance becomes 100.
POST {{host}}/webhooks/payment
X-Signature: {{webhookSig}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{{webhookBody}}

### Balance now 100
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### REPLAY the same webhook (PSPs retry) -> idempotent, balance STILL 100.
POST {{host}}/webhooks/payment
X-Signature: {{webhookSig}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{{webhookBody}}

### FORGED webhook (bad signature) -> 401, no credit.
POST {{host}}/webhooks/payment
X-Signature: deadbeefbadsignature
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{{webhookBody}}

### Declined card -> status Declined, no deposit to credit.
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "paymentToken": "tok_decline", "amount": 50 }

### 3-D Secure card -> RequiresAction + clientSecret (browser completes the challenge).
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "paymentToken": "tok_3ds", "amount": 50 }

### --- IDOR check: a DIFFERENT user cannot touch alice's account ---
# @name loginBob
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "username": "bob", "password": "any-non-empty" }

###
@bobToken = {{loginBob.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Bob reads alice's account -> 403 Forbidden
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### Bob debits alice's account -> 403 Forbidden
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "amount": 10, "idempotencyKey": "bob-steal" }
